fixture_fill — Replace NA with a value, as a fixture                         core · tier 0 · since 0.7.0 · 1.0 · exact

USAGE
    fixture_fill(x, value)

DESCRIPTION
    `value` where `x` is NA and `x` otherwise, for the four scalar types: the fixture of a parameter of
    several types and a result typed `Join`.

ARGUMENTS
    x           Bool | Int | Float | Str. The value, of any scalar type, or a column of them.
    value       Bool | Int | Float | Str. What stands in for NA, of a type that joins with x's.

VALUE
    x or value, of their joined type; a column when x is one.

WARNINGS AND NOTES
    Z0214   the arguments are of types that do not join

ACCURACY
    Exact.

SEE ALSO
    fill_missing, coalesce

EXAMPLES
    > fixture_fill(NA, 3)
    3
    > fixture_fill("a", "b")
    a
